# A whitelist rather than a blacklist, on purpose.
#
# Runs create screenshot directories with ad-hoc names (shots-sonnet5, qwen-a,
# gem-smoke3, calib) holding pictures of a live desktop, alongside traces
# containing entire conversations. A blacklist would quietly commit the next
# name someone invents, and the contents are exactly what should not be
# published: the test machine's screen, including whatever files and windows
# happened to be open.
#
# Add new source paths below explicitly.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/cmake/
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/CMakeLists.txt
!/src/
!/include/
!/docs/
!/third_party/
!/tools/

# tools/make-movie.py is a script, never an import, so a __pycache__ here means
# something loaded it as a module — which is what a test harness does.
/tools/__pycache__/
